SUMMARY
Records ownership_pct, days_available_for_rent and private_use_days for
the financial year already selected on the tax report.

FILES
- app/actions/property-fy-facts.ts (new) - upsertPropertyFyFacts
- components/property-fy-facts-panel.tsx (new) - client form
- app/(dashboard)/properties/[propertyId]/tax-report/page.tsx - fetches
  the year's facts and renders the panel
- lib/tax/fy.ts - added daysInFy
- tests/lib/tax/fy.test.ts - 3 tests for daysInFy (41 total)

DESIGN DECISIONS
- Placed on the tax report because the FY is already selected there;
  a second year picker would be a second source of truth.
- Absent facts are shown as STATED ASSUMPTIONS ("assumes sole ownership
  and available all 365 days"), not pre-filled inputs. Pre-filling would
  present an assumption as a recorded fact - the exact distinction
  product-guidelines.md requires the pack to preserve.
- Authorisation left to RLS. The action checks the session and validates
  ranges for a friendly message, but the database write policy is the
  actual boundary.
- daysInFy extracted into the tested helper rather than computed inline,
  so a leap year reports 366 instead of a hardcoded 365.

VERIFICATION PERFORMED
Upsert semantics (live, local Supabase, as the owner via forged JWT
claims):
  first save                  -> row created (50%, 300 days)
  second save, same year      -> UPDATED in place (75%, 365), not duplicated
  save for a different year   -> separate row; 2026 undisturbed
  viewer attempts same upsert -> DENIED, RLS policy violation
Confirms ON CONFLICT (property_id, financial_year_end) targets the
composite key correctly and that per-year isolation holds.

updated_at trigger: an in-transaction timestamp comparison returned false,
which is a TEST ARTIFACT - now() is constant within a transaction, so
created_at and updated_at are necessarily equal there. Confirmed
separately that trg_property_fy_facts_updated_at exists and calls
set_updated_at, and that clock_timestamp() <> now() inside a transaction.
Not a defect.

npm run build     -> Compiled successfully, no type errors.
CI=true npm test  -> 41 tests passed.

